{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Where is their eloheinu.</b> Israel says: ״Where is their eloheinu?״ Even though their deeds are not blameless, none the less He comes with a claim before Elohim, who is alluded to in the word צור — and He is their refuge. For Israel, even though they transgress and violate some of the mitzvot of HaShem, none the less their entire refuge is in HaShem, and for His sake they endure poverty and lowliness, and they are killed for the sanctification of His name, and they stand and long for the Rock their redeemer — and this is what the verse says, ״their refuge is in Him.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:37.194463658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}